{"id": "EUVD-2026-76268", "enisaUuid": "f1f4b1e7-8dba-3a6b-9cfd-f54ad7fbf132", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: iaa - unmap dst before software fallback on decompress\n\nOn a hardware analytics error, decompress retries through the software\nfallback, which writes req->dst with the CPU while it is still mapped\nDMA_FROM_DEVICE. With SWIOTLB active the later dma_unmap_sg() copies the\nstale bounce buffer over req->dst, corrupting the result.\n\nUnmap before the fallback runs. The async path unmaps inline; the sync\npath signals the retry with -EAGAIN so iaa_comp_adecompress() runs the\nfallback after unmapping.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:29", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c0279e5ea2aad99d8b91f1a6579d751cc9eb2408", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc933a4a419ba8a75da28666a018602c44846953", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fcd86180ef78b0e41763faef7c6d2de7dfb50c1a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94a25930477113730372e0fa2985da4c5ac95c9a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80945", "GHSA-p5w3-q665-q5v8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.5, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b84647e-0def-3d1d-9487-af6649a4fc6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ec6761df889fdf896fde761abd447596dd8f8c2 <94a25930477113730372e0fa2985da4c5ac95c9a"}, {"id": "12e77aae-ed69-3e32-ae3b-0a3f46ac41d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "239e1c9e-d637-3571-a8e3-6ba130682399", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ec6761df889fdf896fde761abd447596dd8f8c2 <fc933a4a419ba8a75da28666a018602c44846953"}, {"id": "407982fe-acc1-32cc-968c-7c654cb6ec5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ec6761df889fdf896fde761abd447596dd8f8c2 <c0279e5ea2aad99d8b91f1a6579d751cc9eb2408"}, {"id": "5a4cff86-8666-3860-9a88-7c06c0b1e2ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ec6761df889fdf896fde761abd447596dd8f8c2 <fcd86180ef78b0e41763faef7c6d2de7dfb50c1a"}, {"id": "7792f7de-c281-39ad-94dd-bcd577161b44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9dab98bc-c884-31b9-9769-d86c7c0dba6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "9df49b79-fee7-3fbb-9d3a-6f3df38f2f3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "afc7f714-eb18-38da-acf0-ab6f7da61177", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "cb9076ad-d3d5-3306-9806-78a1c1fa1ae9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ade628f7-2eb2-3b15-95a2-1b854f877601", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}